.TH ASTRAS-PET-OS 1 2026-10-19 "Astra's PetOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
astras-pet-os \- Astra's PetOS on Linux: your farm of pets, the System Map and Linux Penguin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B astras-pet-os
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B astras-pet-os setup
.RB [ \-\-farm " example|scratch" ]
.RB [ \-\-pets " id,id..." ]
.br
.B astras-pet-os service
.RB { on | off }
.I pet
.SH DESCRIPTION
Astra's PetOS is a platform of small intelligent apps, called pets, organized by the Friendly Farmer.
.B astras-pet-os
sets up your farm, opens its pages, runs Linux Penguin's check of this computer, and turns optional pet services on
and off. The program is read only in
.IR /usr/share/astras-pet-os ;
your farm is in
.IR ~/.local/share/astras-pet-os .
With no command it shows the commands, and Linux Penguin says which Linux this is and which of his tricks fits it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Set up your farm: Astra's example pets, or from scratch (the core pets, plus the pets you pick). Asks when no
.B \-\-farm
is given. Run it again to change the farm.
.TP
.B list\-pets
The pets you can put on your farm, with their ids.
.TP
.BR map ", " desk
Open the System Map, or the Friendly Farmer's desk, in your browser.
.TP
.B penguin
Linux Penguin's read\-only check of this computer: distribution and family, updates waiting, failed services, the SSH
server, disk, memory and anything listening beyond this computer. It never runs sudo.
.TP
.B services
The pet services and whether each is on. They are all off until you turn one on.
.TP
.BI "service on " pet ", service off " pet
Turn a pet service (a systemd user service) on or off. Before turning one on, it checks that the pet's program, its
packages, its settings and its secrets file are there, and says what is missing.
.TP
.B stop
The big red button: stop every pet service now.
.TP
.B version
The version, and where the release is.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/astras-pet-os/farm/
Your farm: its pets.json, draft list and farm\-receipt.json.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/astras-pet-os/pets/
Pet programs you cloned yourself, for pet services.
.TP
.I ~/.config/astras-pet-os/pets/<pet>.env
A pet service's secrets, readable only by you (chmod 600).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/astras-pet-os-pet@.service
The pet service template. The package never turns it on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
